This directory contains code which illustrates polymorphic design using
circuit elements (AC Voltage Source, Capacitor, Resistor, Inductor, Wire)
as examples. These all inherit from CircuitElement. 

With virtual methods in CircuitElement, one can construct circuits out
of these elements.

The CircuitSimulator in this directory is work-in-progress, it is not
ready to be used yet.  It is intended to allow simulation of a
simple multiple-branch circuits built from bipolar devices.
For that, come back later.

A program to build and visualize a circuit can be found in the
CH12/POLYRLC directory.  The visualization code depend on Qt and so
is not part of this library, designed to have no dependencies.

